00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.467
-Are you kidding me?

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.868
-[ Laughing ]
Really?

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:18.834
-I think your name actually --
is it true? --

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.367
came from basketball?

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:21.501
Right?
How you got Suga?

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:24.901
-Yeah.
Shooting guard -- shoo-ga.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:27.234
-Shooting and guard,
so "shoo-ga."

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.601
-"Shoo-ga."
-Yeah.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:31.567
And then,
can you explain Agust D?

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.634
-Yep.
-How? I don't --

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:36.534
-Reverse.
D.T. Suga.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:38.100
[ Cheering ]
-Oh.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:43.033
-Yeah.
My hometown name is Daegu.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:44.501
-Ah, D.T. Suga.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:47.601
-Daegu town Suga.
Reverse.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:50.734
Agust D.
-So that's your hometown, D.T.?

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:53.400
-Yeah, D.T.
-D.T. So, D.T. Suga.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.434
D.T. Suga is pretty cool, too.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:57.467
-But you want to go Agust D?

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.033
-No. Drive-through.
D.T.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:02.834
-Oh, yeah, yeah. Drive-through.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.400
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
I understand, yeah.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.767
Yeah, I understand.
But when -- when you're --

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:10.734
When you're Agust D, are you
different than when you're Suga?

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.767
You are.
Yeah.

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:21.701
-You can call me Agust D
or Suga or Yoongi.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.801
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.968
You answer to all that.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.734
-It's a great record.

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:29.000
Congratulations on this.
What does --

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.167
What does "D-DAY" mean to you?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.601
Wow. It's a big deal.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:54.667
And the song you're
performing tonight is "Haegeum."

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.167
-Mm-hmm.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.267
Not yet.
Soon. Soon.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.801
Not yet, not yet.
Soon, soon, soon.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:05.234
But you were telling me
that "Haegeum" has two meanings.

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:06.868
-Mm-hmm.
Yeah.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:08.467
-What are the meanings
of Haegeum?

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:17.801
Do you --
Do you know how to play haegeum?

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:20.133
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:22.734
-Are you sure?
Because...

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:23.901
-Wow.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.467
I stole it
from your dressing room.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.567
No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:37.067
[ Scraping ]

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.133
Give me that, give me that,
give me that.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.300
Yeah, yeah, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.000
Let me try.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.400
Quest, can I get a beat?

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.968
♪♪

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.501
[ Light scraping ]

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:51.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:57.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.467 --> 00:05:01.501
